# Wave W17-V (Route 206): pillarway sand — the walking road’s pale sand under the pillars: a cool pale sand carrying sparse pillar-stone grey flecks ground off the cycleway’s stone (design-authorised: the walking road runs under the elevated way, mouth to mouth). Split from Maris Route 110’s underdeck sand by the stone dust and the cooler cast: Borea’s pillars are stone, and their road wears it.
